## 1. Component graph

Nine components. Everything left of `MAT` is a per-cell read of prose; everything right of it
is a pure function over a table. That seam is deliberate: it is the only place judgment
enters, so it is the only place bias can enter, and it is fully audited by the `locus`
obligation (§3.3).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    SRC[("SRC — reviews/tasks/&lt;id&gt;_review.md<br/>sealed goal records (read-only)")]
    SEL["SEL — Goal Selector<br/>§2.1 selection rule"]
    SCHEMA["SCHEMA — Extraction Target Schema<br/>§2.2 · 71 cells/goal · FROZEN by this design"]
    EX["EX — Hand Extractor<br/>per (goal × cell)"]
    ADJ["ADJ — Cell Adjudicator<br/>§4.2 disposition FSM"]
    MAT["MAT — Field Verdict Matrix<br/>3 × 71 cells"]
    SCORE["SCORE — Loss Calculator<br/>§5.1 pure"]
    GATE["GATE — Verdict Rule<br/>§5.3 pre-registered predicate"]
    EMIT["EMIT — Report Emitter"]
    OUT[("OUT — reviews/spikes/<br/>sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md")]
    ACC{{"ACC — Acceptance Harness<br/>4 shell assertions (§7)"}}
    SPEC[("SAEOS-1 §4.2 envelope · §4.3 types<br/>§6.1b bundle · PAEOS-9 §5 graphs")]

    SPEC --> SCHEMA
    SRC --> SEL
    SEL -->|"GoalRef ×3"| EX
    SCHEMA -->|"Cell ×71"| EX
    SRC -->|"prose body"| EX
    EX -->|"candidate finding + locus"| ADJ
    ADJ -->|"CellVerdict"| MAT
    MAT --> SCORE
    SCORE -->|"Metrics"| GATE
    GATE -->|"Verdict"| EMIT
    MAT --> EMIT
    SCORE --> EMIT
    SEL -->|"ceremony depth"| EMIT
    EMIT --> OUT
    OUT --> ACC
```

**No orphan.** `SCHEMA` is consumed by `EX`; every `Cell` it emits reaches `MAT`; every `MAT`
cell reaches both `SCORE` and `EMIT`; `SEL`'s ceremony-depth output reaches `EMIT` (it is not
decorative — it drives the `n/a-auto-discharged` exclusion, §4.2). `ACC` is the terminal
consumer and is the only component this design does not author (it is fixed by the gate).

**No gap.** The three acceptance-visible outputs — `verdict`, `loss_ratio`, and three
`## goal:` sections — each have exactly one producer: `GATE`, `SCORE`, `SEL`+`EMIT`.

