## 3. Data flow

### 3.1 End to end

```
reviews/tasks/<id>_review.md   (prose, sealed)
        │  SEL: filter sealed · maximise ceremony diversity
        ▼
GoalRef ×3  { task_id, path, ceremony_depth }
        │  × SCHEMA's 71 cells
        ▼
(goal, node_type, field)  ── EX: locate in source ──▶ candidate finding + locus
        │
        ▼  ADJ: §4.2 FSM
CellVerdict { disposition, locus|searched, note }
        │
        ▼
Matrix 3×71  ──▶ SCORE ──▶ Metrics ──▶ GATE ──▶ Verdict
        │                     │                    │
        └─────────────────────┴────────────────────┴──▶ EMIT ──▶ spike report ──▶ ACC
```

### 3.2 Dispositions

Five dispositions. Three are **verdicts** (in the denominator, per the objective); two are
**exclusions** (out of the denominator, each requiring a stated justification).

| Disposition | Score `s` | In denominator | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `extractable` | 1.0 | ✅ | Present and mechanically locatable — a parser could find it |
| `partial` | 0.5 | ✅ | Present but prose-embedded / ambiguous / needs judgment — **mechanical loss**, fixable by a better extractor |
| `absent` | 0.0 | ✅ | Not in the artifact at all — **structural loss**, fixable only by changing what PAEOS emits |
| `n/a-synthesized` | — | ❌ | Assigned at ingest, never extracted (§2.2 list of 10) |
| `n/a-auto-discharged` | — | ❌ | The producing L-stage was pruned by ceremony depth (Trace-A, PAEOS-9 §8.3) — measures triage, not extractability |

The `partial` / `absent` split is the probe's core instrument. A8 asks whether PAEOS artifacts
are "too unstructured to extract losslessly." Prose-but-present is exactly the loss S1's
extractor exists to eliminate; genuinely-missing is loss no extractor can touch. Collapsing
them into one number would make the probe unable to answer the question it was commissioned
to answer.

### 3.3 The `locus` obligation

Every `extractable` or `partial` cell MUST carry a `locus`: a section anchor or ≤ 120-char
quotation from the source review. Every `absent` cell MUST carry a `searched` note naming
where it was looked for. Every exclusion MUST carry its justification.

This mirrors SAEOS-1 §5.1 rule 2 — *"Every result carries `why` … an unexplainable result is
a defect."* An unsourced `extractable` is unfalsifiable optimism; an unsearched `absent` is
unfalsifiable pessimism. Either one silently decides GO/NO-GO.

