## 4. State machines

### 4.1 Probe lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PREREGISTERED: thresholds frozen by this design (§5.3)
    PREREGISTERED --> SELECTING: read reviews/tasks/
    SELECTING --> INSUFFICIENT: <3 sealed goals, or §2.1 rule 2 unsatisfiable
    SELECTING --> EXTRACTING: 3 GoalRefs bound
    EXTRACTING --> EXTRACTING: next (goal × cell) — 213 iterations
    EXTRACTING --> SCORED: matrix complete (every cell has a disposition)
    SCORED --> ADJUDICATED: GATE evaluates G1..G5
    INSUFFICIENT --> ADJUDICATED: forced NO-GO, scope=insufficient-sample
    ADJUDICATED --> EMITTED: report written to reviews/spikes/
    EMITTED --> [*]: ACC runs the 4 assertions

    note right of EXTRACTING
      No exit while any cell is UNSEEN.
      An incomplete matrix is not a low
      score — it is not a result at all.
    end note
    note right of ADJUDICATED
      GO   → S1 build authorised (SAEOS-1 §8)
      NO-GO→ remand to SAEOS-1 §6.1b / §8;
             A8's carried risk is realised
    end note
```

`INSUFFICIENT` routes to `ADJUDICATED`, not to `[*]`: an aborted probe still owes a report and
a verdict. Silence is not a NO-GO, and a NO-GO is not a failure — a falsification test that
falsifies has succeeded.

### 4.2 Per-cell adjudication

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> UNSEEN
    UNSEEN --> EXCLUDED_SYNTH: field ∈ §2.2 synthesized set
    UNSEEN --> EXCLUDED_CEREMONY: producing L-stage auto-discharged (Trace-A)
    UNSEEN --> SEARCHING: otherwise
    SEARCHING --> LOCATED: found in source
    SEARCHING --> NOT_FOUND: exhaustive search, nothing
    LOCATED --> EXTRACTABLE: unambiguous + mechanically addressable
    LOCATED --> PARTIAL: present but prose-embedded / ambiguous / needs judgment
    NOT_FOUND --> ABSENT: record `searched:`
    EXCLUDED_SYNTH --> [*]
    EXCLUDED_CEREMONY --> [*]
    EXTRACTABLE --> [*]
    PARTIAL --> [*]
    ABSENT --> [*]

    note right of LOCATED
      Mandatory: locus (anchor or ≤120-char quote).
      No locus ⇒ the cell may not leave LOCATED.
    end note
```

**Ordering is normative.** Exclusion tests run *before* search, so a Trace-A-pruned field is
never scored as `absent`. Reversing the order is the single most likely way to produce a
spurious NO-GO, because it silently converts a triage decision into evidence about
extractability.

Every state has an entry and a terminal exit; `UNSEEN` is the only entry; there is no state
from which a cell can leave the machine without a disposition.

